    },
    {
      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "When an employer intends to close or cease operations, it must give a written notice to the workers and the Ministry of Labor and Employment at least one (1) month before the intended date. If the termination is due to installation of labor‑saving devices or redundancy, the employee gets separation pay of at least one (1) month pay or one (1) month pay for each year of service, whichever is higher. If the termination is for retrenchment to prevent losses or for closure not caused by serious business losses or financial reverses, the separation pay is one (1) month pay or at least one‑half (½) month pay for each year of service, whichever is higher, with any fraction of at least six (6) months counted as a whole year.",
