{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "For a covered employee, the law requires that every employer give a rest period of at least twenty‑four (24) consecutive hours after each stretch of six consecutive normal work days. This rest day must be provided before any work can be required on that day, unless an emergency or other exceptional condition specified in a separate provision applies.",
