    {
      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "Where a service supplier provides a service that is imperfect—meaning it is not fit for its intended purpose or does not match the advertised description—the supplier is liable. The consumer may choose one of three remedies: (1) have the service performed again at no extra cost; (2) receive an immediate refund of the amount paid, with monetary updating; or (3) obtain a proportionate reduction in price. The supplier may also have a qualified third party redo the service, but the risk and cost remain with the supplier.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_002.s1.q1"
        },
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_002.s1.q2"
        },
