        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Ayon sa Labor Advisory No. 06‑2020, dapat ibigay ng employer ang final pay ng empleyado within 30 days mula siya umalis, maliban kung may mas pabor na patakaran ang kumpanya. Ang Certificate of Employment naman ay dapat ibigay within three days mula hilingin ng empleyado. Ang “better policy” ay isang kondisyon na kailangang nakasulat at mas pabor sa manggagawa kaysa sa default na 30‑day rule.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_001.s1.q3"
        },
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_001.s1.q4"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "Sa ilalim ng Art. 102 ng Consumer Act, kung hindi maayos ang repair service, may tatlong opsyon ang consumer: (1) ipagawa ulit ang serbisyo nang walang dagdag na bayad; (2) hingin ang agarang refund ng bayad kasama ang monetary updating; o (3) humingi ng proportionate price reduction. Ang pagpili ay depende sa consumer, at ang re‑performance ng serbisyo puwedeng ipasa sa qualified third party na sagot ng supplier.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_002.s4.q1"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Under the Omnibus Rules, a worker may be dismissed only for a just or authorized cause and only after due process. Due process requires the employer to give the worker a written notice that specifies the acts or omissions that are the grounds for dismissal, and the worker must be allowed a reasonable period to answer those allegations. The employer must also afford the worker ample opportunity to be heard and to defend himself, with a representative if desired.",
      "evidence": [
