      "text": "For any employee who works between 10 p.m. and 6 a.m., the law requires the employer to pay a night‑shift differential of at least 10 % of the employee’s regular wage for each hour worked, unless the employee falls under the exemptions listed in Section 1 (government workers, establishments with five or fewer workers, domestic helpers, managerial staff, or workers engaged on a task‑ or commission‑only basis without supervised time).",
