      "text": "Under Section 14 of the Omnibus Rules, an employer may deduct wages for loss or damage only if (1) the business is in a trade, occupation or industry where such deductions are a recognized practice, (2) the employee is clearly shown to be responsible for the loss or damage, and (3) the employee is given a reasonable opportunity to explain why the deduction should not be made; the deduction must also be fair, not exceed the actual loss, and cannot be more than 20 % of the employee’s weekly wages. Because the private business intends to deduct alleged stock loss without first establishing the employee’s responsibility or giving that chance to be heard, the deduction does not satisfy the statutory conditions and may be considered an unlawful withholding of wages.",
